<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Rooms &amp; Exits</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Chapter 2</a> &gt; Level 18</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 18 Walkthrough: Sports Store</h1>

    <p class="lede">The Sports Store is a shop, a gym and a billiards corner in one open floor, and it hides both of its codes in plain sight — seven cap colours on a wall for the till, five numbered billiard balls for the exit. Read it in the order the room wants: sweep the floor for tools, build the drill, read the caps, then walk to the back and count the balls. The whole run is under nine minutes if you know where to look, and most of that time is a sliding-block puzzle you do not actually need.</p>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Rebuilt frame by frame from two independent recordings of the current build — a full 8:57 playthrough extracted at one frame per second, with four frames per second through the last two door attempts, and a second complete playthrough of the same room used as a second read. Every code printed here was read off the screen at least twice: the till passcode <b>6273519</b> agrees across four separate readings (two per recording), and the exit code <b>84371</b> is read from the ball display and again from the keypad in both runs. One number on this page — the racket count <b>5216</b> — comes from a single recording and is labelled as such rather than presented as a constant. Anything we could not read twice is listed under "What this page could not verify" instead of being printed as fact. On-screen text was read with optical character recognition on the raw frames, not typed by hand, and every step timestamp points at the exact second in the embedded video.</div>

    <LevelSelector chapter={2} current={18} variant="jump" label="Chapter 2 · No Honor Among Thieves" />

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>The exit keypad takes <b>84371</b>, read straight off the five billiard balls in the glass display beside it — <b>8 · 4 · 3 · 7 · 1</b>. The till on the shop floor takes <b>6273519</b>, built from the seven cap colours on the wall. Finish pays <b>+5 coins</b> with the clock at <b>8:39</b>.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Take the loose gear on the floor: <b>Football</b>, <b>Fastening tool</b>, <b>Screw</b>, <b>Billiard balls</b>. Combine the tool and the bit, then the screw, into a <b>Fastening tool with a screw</b>.</li>
        <li>Read the <b>seven caps</b> on the slatwall (red, orange, yellow, blue, green, pink, pale blue) and press the same colours on the <b>keypad</b> beside the counter → <b>6273519</b>.</li>
        <li>Type the code into the checkout monitor's <b>ENTER PASSCODE</b> screen; the counter pays out its blue "done" screen.</li>
        <li>Clear the <b>gym slide puzzle</b> (a scrambled picture with one empty square) → <b>Key</b>. Cut the last billiard ball out of the <b>punching bag</b> base with the <b>Knife</b> (counter 5/6 → 6/6).</li>
        <li>Match the <b>hoodie icons</b> to the <b>six icon balls</b> — "Look at the icons not colour" is the game's own hint — and deal with the <b>bottle</b> colour order.</li>
        <li>Read the <b>five billiard balls</b> in the display: <b>8 · 4 · 3 · 7 · 1</b>. Type <b>84371</b> into the keypad on the same stand, press the green tick, and walk out.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
            <div class="yt-facade" data-yt="IG5w4lWVk3I" data-title="Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 18 Sports Store walkthrough"
           role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play video: Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 18 Sports Store walkthrough">
